  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  storyPanel: {fileID: 912955754}
  storyText: {fileID: 1015657730}
  storyCanvasGroup: {fileID: 912955758}
  baseBackgroundImage: {fileID: 660484216}
  fadeBackgroundImage: {fileID: 1048599734}
  fadeImageCanvasGroup: {fileID: 1048599731}
  storyPages:
  - The voyage across the Atlantic was supposed to be a routine cargo run. The steel
    hull was strong, and the lower decks were packed with supplies, tools, and materials.
    We had everything we needed for a safe trip. Until the storm hit.
  - The waves ripped the ship apart in minutes. Metal groaned and wood splintered
    as the freezing water pulled us under. I grabbed onto a broken piece of the deck,
    helplessly watching all our cargo and raw materials scatter into the dark ocean.
  - Morning. The storm is gone, leaving me stranded on a few planks of wood. But
    the ocean is full of drifting debris. If I can just hook that junk and tie it
    together, I can expand this raft. I can build a way to survive.
  storyBackgrounds:
  - {fileID: 21300000, guid: 08a29ae47a83db645be02bce102fbee6, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 21300000, guid: 75473beb299ebcc408bc0f060c4e7fa5, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 21300000, guid: bfcdae768e208d349995c3dfd388f848, type: 3}
  fadeInDuration: 1
  typingSpeed: 0.08
  backgroundCrossfadeDuration: 0.8
  mainMenuScript: {fileID: 561395775}
